{
  "_comment": [
    "Coinbase Derivatives contract specifications.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the funding parser computed notional as contracts * price,",
    "which is the identity only for a contract whose unit is one unit of the underlying.",
    "Twelve HEP contracts at $0.0802 is $4,812 of notional, not $0.96, and every figure",
    "downstream inherited the 5,000x error at full confidence.",
    "",
    "PERPETUAL IS NOT DATED. The parser recovers a funding rate, and only a",
    "perpetual-style contract has funding. BIP/ETP/SLP/XPP/HEP debit and credit open",
    "positions via a funding rate; BIT/ET/SOL/HED and the rest are dated futures that",
    "expire and pay no funding. A matching multiplier does not make them the same",
    "instrument: ET and ETP are both 0.1 ETH and only one of them has a rate to recover.",
    "The dated rows are here for contract conversion only and are excluded from the",
    "parser in code, not by convention.",
    "",
    "SOURCES ARE PRIMARY. Every row is read off the product table in the CFTC",
    "self-certification filing cited in source_documents, which lists product name,",
    "contract code and contract size together. The five perpetuals additionally carry",
    "Coinbase's own published specification sheet, which states the funding mechanism",
    "in terms. Nothing here comes from press coverage.",
    "",
    "THIS TABLE IS A SNAPSHOT, NOT A CENSUS. It is the product list as it stood in the",
    "filing dated 2025-11-26. Coinbase has listed contracts since, and lists many assets",
    "this board scores that are absent here. An absent symbol therefore means NO VERIFIED",
    "CONTRACT MAPPING, which is not the same claim as no contract existing, and the",
    "terminal is required to say the former. Saying the latter would be inventing a fact",
    "about the exchange out of a gap in this file.",
    "",
    "A SYMBOL ABSENT FROM THIS FILE HAS AN UNKNOWN MULTIPLIER, NOT A MULTIPLIER OF 1.",
    "Note that 1 is a real contract size here: BTI is 1 BTC and BCH is 1 BCH. That is",
    "exactly why the silent default was dangerous rather than merely wrong, and why a",
    "user-entered multiplier marks every figure it produces as unverified."
  ],
